msgid "File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:67
msgid ""
"The full path of file containing location (GPS) data. Supported extensions "
"are ``.gpx`` and ``.tcx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:68
msgid "Time offset in seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:69
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:72
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:75
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:81
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:90
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:96
msgid "Integer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:70
msgid ""
"An offset to be added to the video file to match it to the GPS track. Most "
"of the time this will at least need to be set to the timezone difference "
"between the two files plus some seconds if the video recording device is not "
"precisely set to the correct time. GPS time is always exact and in UTC\\ "
"[#]_. Use positive values if GPS is ahead of video, and negative otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:71
msgid "Smoothing level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:73
msgid ""
"Determines how many GPS points to smooth in order to eliminate GPS errors. A "
"value of 0 only exposes the raw values from the file. A value of 1 does not "
"smooth locations, it only calculates the extra fields (speed, distance, etc) "
"it also interpolates missing values for **heart rate** and **altitude**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:74
msgid "Updates per second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/generate/gps_text.rst:76
msgid ""
"Controls how many times per second the GPS text is updated on video "
"(interpolated). A value of 0 will only update text when a real GPS point has "
"been recorded."
msgstr ""

